+### Output and Pipeline Delays
+
+The output and pipeline delays of an H.264 or HEVC stream add up to 13 frames,
+and the picture size the client configures decides the split (*DecodeDelays.h*).
+The framework reads them once when it starts, so the size the device later states
+for the stream (its SPS) changes neither: a stream configured at 1080p whose SPS
+declares 4K keeps the 12 capture buffers it was sized for, and one configured at
+4K whose SPS declares 1080p keeps 8.
+
 ### Picture Size
 
 *C2_PARAMKEY_PICTURE_SIZE* takes any even width and height from 16 up and
